    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "## Problem\n\nRan a non-ephemeral `:terminal` command super zoomed in. I zoom out - no\nreflow!! The text is choped off.\n\n(I think) this is because Neovim skips terminal resizing when the terminal is\nclosed.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim --clean` in a term w/ >= 80 cols\n2. Run:\n\n   ```vim\n   vnew\n   vertical resize 20\n   call jobstart(['sh', '-c', 'printf \"%s\\n\" \"012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789\"'], {'term': v:true})\n   ```\n\n3. Wait for process to exit\n4. Widen:\n\n   ```vim\n   vertical resize 70\n   ```\n\n5. Witness the output being split:\n\n```text\n01234567890123456789\n01234567890123456789\n01234567890123456789\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nOutput is recombined in one row:\n\n```text\n012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789\n```\n\n## Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-nightly+95df8c0\n\n## Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\n[Vim version and behavior]\n\n## Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 26.5.1 (25F80)\n\n## Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1\n\n## $TERM environment variable\n\n`xterm-256color`\n\n## Installation\n\nNix, through `neovim-nightly-overlay`.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
